.Dd March 12, 2026
.Dt PCI_DEVICE 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pci_device_create
.Nd create and register a PCI function with the kernel driver model
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/pci.h
.Ft pci_device_t *
.Fn pci_device_create "uint8_t bus" "uint8_t slot" "uint8_t func"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn pci_device_create
function reads identification fields for the specified PCI function, allocates
a
.Vt pci_device_t ,
creates a corresponding
.Vt struct device ,
and registers that kernel device on the global
.Dq pci
bus type.
.Pp
The created
.Vt struct device
is populated with PCI vendor, device, class, subclass, and programming
interface identifiers so the generic driver model can match it against PCI
driver ID tables.
.Pp
If a matching driver is already registered on the PCI bus,
.Fn pci_device_create
also invokes the normal device probe path.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn pci_device_create
function returns the created
.Vt pci_device_t
on success or
.Dv NULL
if the function is absent or allocation/registration fails.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr device_register 9 ,
.Xr device_probe 9 ,
.Xr pci_scan 9
